{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1707"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1707: URL credential redaction strips host and path from public URLs with @ in the path, and a stored credential-bearing identity is echoed verbatim in claim refusals"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1707 (filed 2026-11-11). Two gaps in the URL-credential redaction shipped by pm-nhauur. (1) Over-redaction: the rule replaces everything between a token's first colon and its last at-sign, so a public URL without userinfo but with an at-sign in the path loses its host and path; an npm scoped-package URL becomes https://[redacted]@unbrained/pm-cli and the retry command is useless. Proposal: treat a URL as carrying userinfo only when, after the double slash, an at-sign appears before the first slash, question mark or hash, or a colon appears before the first slash and an at-sign appears later; keep the conservative span for real userinfo, including a slash inside a base64 password. (2) Under-redaction of stored identities: PM_AUTHOR set to a credential URL with whitespace in the userinfo is accepted as author, assignee and claim_principal without any secret-guard advisory, persisted, and echoed verbatim three times in a later claim refusal, because the invocation-scoped registry only covers the current argv. Proposal: identity fields refuse or strip URL userinfo at write time, refusal builders redact stored identity values with the same rule as argv, and older data still reads. pm-rust mirrors the fixed behaviour already (pm-rust#165)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1707","privacy","redaction","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A URL is redacted only when it carries userinfo (an at-sign before the first slash, question mark or hash after the scheme, or a colon before the first slash and a later at-sign); npm scoped-package and GitHub blob URLs with an at-sign in the path survive intact; Real userinfo stays redacted, including a slash inside a base64 password, a bare token user and a multi-colon password; Identity fields (author, assignee, claim principal from flags or PM_AUTHOR) refuse or strip URL userinfo at write time; Refusal builders redact stored identity values with the argv rule, including whitespace inside userinfo; data written by older versions still reads"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Public URLs survive redaction and no stored credential reaches a refusal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Scoped-package URLs lose host and path; a credential identity is echoed three times"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1699","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-nhauur","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4a2dfc5c25ca6eec7c5f95ae9c7b04c02ffcdbe45bee81b4b425bef1ec90cc4a","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d4cf0f047ea0fd26176159a00d776aa9eeba61f06aab5afb48fe9bbd8379fe9f"}
